  "notes": "The late-2000s end of the pop-punk wave, and slower than the 2002 norm: 82–171 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the signature single at 86 in F minor, which is where `bpm.mode` sits. The kit is \"tightly gridded and mixed loud\" by a producer who also mixed the record, so `quantizeStrength` is 0.96 — the hardest grid in this batch — against a loud accent tier. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick 1 and the '&' of 2\", \"snare 2&4 with a short bright crack\", and \"a one-bar 16th tom fill into each chorus\" with \"breakdowns drop to kick-and-clap\", which is the tom-led perc block, a 4-bar fill schedule and a high `dropOutBeats`. Harmony is F minor and other flat minors over i–VI–III–VII and i–VII–VI, \"power-chord voicings with an open-string drone\", so the triad share is high and the voicing is open. The identity instrument is \"a syncopated palm-muted riff\", which is the `riff_loop` melody structure and the answer-lick counter — \"the chorus hook is a repeated 2-bar cell answered by the guitar\". The lead spans a documented F3–E♭5 \"with a raspy belt at the top\". ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability.",
